{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-finite-locally-free}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e7ca3ad310d7beb71366014d19fc94320fb773e256ffc6aa3146d68dc5c83062", "source_text": "Locally free modules", "source_text_hash": "sha256:afbe63328af507fcc84e8f6c1c68a6f35308be2faee90e264fa2884e155d9fc5", "unit_id": "tag:05P1:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:08df7f0582f62c0bc7633498f6928e80e8596b3646363534c509b5fe368b727e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ac4925216e5917ace8378b6dcfcff4424e4aee44e30938c4ba749a709c62de8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOn any ringed space we know what it means for an <MATH_0001>-module\nto be (finite) locally free. On an affine scheme this matches the notion\ndefined in the algebra chapter.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f0cc9165bde19712043684a35e58855e8bfcf5cc669b3d183485bd3f15a5efe3", "unit_id": "tag:05P1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = \\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} = \\widetilde{M}$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$M$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$M$", "MATH_0008": "$R$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-free-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8d706d5f712fa8a78e6aa1644b266bd695be962363cfdabf6a28dfff20718dcd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:37b91472a9c3c4d76bc2115fdc465c513e939686857d48cd10880fb9ce8d825c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> for some <MATH_0003>-module <MATH_0004>.\nThe quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0005> is a (finite) locally free\n<MATH_0006>-module of if and only if <MATH_0007> is a (finite)\nlocally free <MATH_0008>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:741498f1cb12209f6ea4978d0811cf0ff483ad5976a62ea2128cd7b3183cba8d", "unit_id": "tag:05JM:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-definition-locally-free}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-definition-locally-free}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c1f7ebf3dd40a64e4ebac05405ae651f459166794212e33fd7f628d623999631", "source_text": "Follows from the definitions, see\nModules, Definition <REF_0001>\nand\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:27ac3fb2023ce3f72215164cc32b5bdaa987ffe290d77713de5289a32b1e8e0a", "unit_id": "tag:05JM:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:32232d4e357d661a9e94dddc9b8ab78ccca80452de918175a1180f542a291f89", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can characterize finite locally free modules in many different ways.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:45b60c89bc755007f247a46eff43aa18355160dd2a50a96f6eb2b665a66caed2", "unit_id": "tag:05P1:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0017": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\rho_\\mathcal{F} : X \\to \\mathbf{Z}, \\quad\nx \\longmapsto\n\\dim_{\\kappa(x)} \\mathcal{F}_x \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}} \\kappa(x)\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-locally-free}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60107bb50442fc931866102df2769e12667f1dfe7631703c5fed98bf9b872181", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2982634f49d5845c5be0494759780d5608fcb1336ee46ba707880521402a61eb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is a flat <MATH_0005>-module of finite presentation,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> is <MATH_0007>-module of finite presentation and\nfor all <MATH_0008> the stalk <MATH_0009> is a free\n<MATH_0010>-module,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0011> is a locally free, finite type <MATH_0012>-module,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0013> is a finite locally free <MATH_0014>-module, and\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0015> is an <MATH_0016>-module of finite type,\nfor every <MATH_0017> the stalk <MATH_0018> is a free\n<MATH_0019>-module, and the function\n<MATH_0020>\nis locally constant in the Zariski topology on <MATH_0021>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f26c8d80b9dbbfca41e1a6f085ba70f2a99d65c70ce79b19d3a46a0df7ac9369", "unit_id": "tag:05P2:statement"}
